PHASE 3 – DEMO INSTRUCTIONS

Step 1 – Open the Project

Open the library-book-checkout project folder using Visual Studio Code.


Step 2 – Run the System

Open the index.html file and select "Open with Live Server."


Step 3 – Open the Dashboard

The Library Book Checkout System will open in the browser and display the Dashboard.


Step 4 – View Books

Navigate to the Books page to view the list of books and their current availability.


Step 5 – Checkout a Book

Go to the Checkout page.

Select a library user.

Select an available book.

Enter or confirm the checkout date and due date.

Complete the checkout transaction.


Step 6 – Verify the Checkout

Check the current checkout records and verify that the selected book is now marked as borrowed.


Step 7 – Return a Book

Go to the Return page.

Find the borrowed book.

Click the Return button.

Confirm that the return transaction is successful.


Step 8 – Verify Book Availability

Go back to the Books page.

Verify that the returned book is now marked as available.


Step 9 – View Users

Go to the Users page to view the registered library users.


Expected Result

The system should successfully display books and users, record book checkouts, process book returns, update book availability, and preserve prototype data using browser localStorage.